From 1c18818cf993cd41fb15630cb786c65184aaa7ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 19:45:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] TFEL, MFront: error reporting in host and device code,
 portable test laws

- `tfel::fail` throws an exception of the given type on the host and
  returns `false` in device code, where exceptions are not supported. The
  calling code block returns this value.
- `TinyNonLinearSolverBase::abortResolution` makes the non linear solver
  fail. Returning `false` from the evaluation of the residual only reduces
  the Newton correction, whereas an exception aborts the resolution.
- `abortIntegration` (Runge-Kutta DSLs) makes the integration fail.
  Returning `false` from `@Derivative` only reduces the time step.

30 test behaviours and models of `mfront/tests` used exceptions, standard
streams or messages built at runtime in their code blocks. They now use
`tfel::fail`, and `abortResolution` when the error is reported during the
resolution of the implicit system. The standard streams and the messages
built at runtime are only used on the host. The behaviour on the host is
unchanged: the same exceptions, with the same messages, are thrown.
